.ds up \fIulp\fR
.SH NAME
sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan, atan2 \- trigonometric functions
and their inverses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <math.h>

double
sin(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
cos(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
tan(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
asin(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
acos(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
atan(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
atan2(\fdouble y\fP, \fIdouble x\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sin ,
.B cos
and 
.B tan
return trigonometric functions of radian arguments \fIx\fP.
.PP
.B asin
returns the arc sine in the range 
.Pi /2 \-
to
.Pi /2.
.PP
.B acos
returns the arc cosine in the range 0 to
.Pi.
.PP
.B atan
returns the arc tangent in the range
.Pi /2 \-
to
.Pi /2.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
math(3), hypot(3), sqrt(3)
.SH AUTHOR
Robert P. Corbett, W. Kahan, Stuart\0I.\0McDonald, Peter\0Tang and,
for the codes for IEEE 754, Dr. Kwok\-Choi\0Ng.
